32z\"><\/path><\/svg><\/span>\n\t\t<\/span>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/summary>\n\t\t\t\t<div role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"e-n-accordion-item-1712\" class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-63f9bce4 e-con-full e-flex wpr-particle-no wpr-jarallax-no wpr-parallax-no wpr-sticky-section-no wpr-column-slider-no wpr-equal-height-no e-con e-child\" data-id=\"63f9bce4\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-22389c08 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"22389c08\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As your <\/span><b>neck and shoulder pain doctor<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, I tell my patients to look for &#8220;Red Flags&#8221;: if you have sudden weakness in your arms, difficulty walking, or if the pain is so severe it prevents sleep, you should see us immediately.<\/span><\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/details>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<details id=\"e-n-accordion-item-1713\" class=\"e-n-accordion-item\" >\n\t\t\t\t<summary class=\"e-n-accordion-item-title\" data-accordion-index=\"4\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-controls=\"e-n-accordion-item-1713\" >\n\t\t\t\t\t<span class='e-n-accordion-item-title-header'><div class=\"e-n-accordion-item-title-text\"> What is the best pillow for neck pain? <\/div><\/span>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class='e-n-accordion-item-title-icon'>\n\t\t\t<span class='e-opened' ><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"e-font-icon-svg e-fas-minus\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\"><path d=\"M416 208H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h384c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z\"><\/path><\/svg><\/span>\n\t\t\t<span class='e-closed'><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"e-font-icon-svg e-fas-plus\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\" xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2000\/svg\"><path d=\"M416 208H272V64c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32h-32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v144H32c-17.67 0-32 14.33-32 32v32c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h144v144c0 17.67 14.33 32 32 32h32c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32V304h144c17.67 0 32-14.33 32-32v-32c0-17.67-14.33-32-32-32z\"><\/path><\/svg><\/span>\n\t\t<\/span>\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/summary>\n\t\t\t\t<div role=\"region\" aria-labelledby=\"e-n-accordion-item-1713\" class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-5197df9 e-flex e-con-boxed wpr-particle-no wpr-jarallax-no wpr-parallax-no wpr-sticky-section-no wpr-column-slider-no wpr-equal-height-no e-con e-child\" data-id=\"5197df9\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-32566cb5 elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"32566cb5\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Generally, a pillow that keeps your neck &#8220;neutral&#8221;\u2014meaning it&#8217;s in a straight line with your spine\u2014is best. Whether you sleep on your side or back, the goal is to prevent your head from tilting too far up or down.<\/span><\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/details>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-37d0f411 e-flex e-con-boxed wpr-particle-no wpr-jarallax-no wpr-parallax-no wpr-sticky-section-no wpr-column-slider-no wpr-equal-height-no e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"37d0f411\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4c464512 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"4c464512\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">Conclusion: Let\u2019s Get You Moving Again<\/h2>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-8eb65da elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"8eb65da\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You don\u2019t have to live a life &#8220;on hold.&#8221; You don&#8217;t have to miss out on the weekend desert trips or the evening walks at the Marina because of a nagging ache.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The journey to a pain-free life begins with a single, courageous step: reaching out for help. Whether it\u2019s a simple strain or a complex condition, we will find the answer together.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">I invite you to join our family of patients who have rediscovered their freedom. Your neck and shoulders carry a lot for you. it\u2019s time we took care of them.<\/span><\/p><p><b>I am ready when you are!<\/b><b><br \/><\/b><b><a href=\"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/contact\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Book an appointment now<\/a> and let\u2019s end the pain together.<\/b><\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3067eda5 e-flex e-con-boxed wpr-particle-no wpr-jarallax-no wpr-parallax-no wpr-sticky-section-no wpr-column-slider-no wpr-equal-height-no e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"3067eda5\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-4d183a6e elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"4d183a6e\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h3 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">References<\/h3>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-3b10f8fb elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"3b10f8fb\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<ol><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><a href=\"https:\/\/orthoinfo.aaos.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">American Academy of Orthopaedic Surgeons (AAOS) &#8211; Neck Pain<\/span><\/a><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.mayoclinic.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mayo Clinic &#8211; Cervical Spondylosis<\/span><\/a><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><a href=\"https:\/\/my.clevelandclinic.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cleveland Clinic &#8211; Neck Pain and Problems<\/span><\/a><\/li><\/ol>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>When you wake up in the morning and find that you cannot turn your head to greet your spouse, or when a sharp, stabbing sensation shoots from your neck down to your fingertips while you&#8217;re playing with your children, the world can suddenly feel very small. I see it every day in my clinic: the look of exhaustion in a father\u2019s eyes because he can\u2019t sit at his desk without agony, or the worry on a mother\u2019s face because she can\u2019t lift her toddler. If you are feeling this way, I want you to take a deep breath and know one thing: I am here to help you.\u00a0 We don&#8217;t just see a &#8220;cervical spine&#8221; or a &#8220;rotator cuff.&#8221; We see a person whose life has been interrupted by pain. Finding the right neck and shoulder pain doctor isn&#8217;t just about finding someone with a diploma on the wall; it\u2019s about finding a partner who will listen to your story, treat your pain with the same urgency they would for their own brother, and guide you back to the life you love in our vibrant city of Dubai. Why Neck and Shoulder Pain Often Travel Together It is rare to find one without the other. Our bodies are beautifully and complexly connected. The neck (cervical spine) is the bridge between your mind and your body, supporting the weight of your head while allowing you to look at the wonders of the Burj Khalifa or the smiles of your family. When something goes wrong in the neck, the shoulders often take the &#8220;blame.&#8221; This is called referred pain. Because the nerves that travel to your arms and shoulders originate in your neck, an irritation at the &#8220;source&#8221; can feel like a fire in your shoulder blade. Common causes of neck and shoulder pain The &#8220;Tech-Neck&#8221; Epidemic: In Dubai&#8217;s fast-paced digital world, we spend hours looking down at phones or hunched over laptops. This puts immense pressure on the delicate structures of the neck. Muscle Strains: Simple things, like a stiff neck from an awkward sleeping position or a sudden jerk while driving in busy traffic, can cause micro-tears in the muscles. The UAE Lifestyle: Whether it&#8217;s the sudden temperature shifts from the summer heat into heavy air conditioning or the physical stress of frequent travel, our environment plays a role in how our muscles tension up. Additional connected symptoms other than neck and shoulder pain As a neck and shoulder pain doctor, I believe the first step in healing is listening. Your symptoms are your body\u2019s way of asking for help. Are You Experiencing These? The Dull Ache: A constant heaviness in the tops of your shoulders that feels like you&#8217;re carrying the weight of the world. Sharp, Shooting Electric Shocks: Pain that zaps down your arm when you move your head a certain way. Numbness or Pins and Needles: A tingling sensation in your hands that makes it hard to grip a coffee cup or type. The Hingeless Feeling: Stiffness that makes it impossible to check your blind spot while driving or look up at the ceiling. If these sound familiar, it is time to move beyond temporary rubs and creams. You deserve a definitive answer. Read also about shoulder blade pain treatment in Dubai with Dr. Usama Saleh. Dr. Usama\u2019s Approach: The Compassionate Diagnosis Pathway When you come to see me, we start with a conversation. I want to know when the pain started, what makes it better, and- most importantly- what it is stopping you from doing. Detailed History: We talk about your lifestyle, your work, and your hobbies. The Physical Exam: I gently check your reflexes, muscle strength, and exactly where the tenderness lies. I want to see how your &#8220;musculoskeletal family&#8221; is working together. State-of-the-Art Imaging: If we need to see deeper, we use: X-Rays: To look at the alignment of your bones and check for arthritis. MRI Scans: To see the soft tissues\u2014the discs, nerves, and ligaments\u2014that don&#8217;t show up on X-rays. EMG (Nerve Tests): To see if a &#8220;pinched nerve&#8221; is the reason your hand feels weak. Treatment Options for neck and shoulder pain I am a firm believer that surgery is the last resort, not the first. As your neck and shoulder pain doctor, my goal is to exhaust every gentle, conservative option before we ever discuss the operating room. Conservative (Non-Surgical) Healing Most of my patients find relief through a combination of: Specialized Physiotherapy: Not just generic exercises, but movements designed to re-educate your posture and strengthen your core. Ergonomic Coaching: We look at how you sit, sleep, and stand. Sometimes, a simple change in your desk height or pillow can be the cure. Advanced Pain Management: This might include targeted injections to calm an inflamed nerve or dry needling to release a stubborn muscle knot. When Surgery Becomes a Necessary Friend In cases where there is severe nerve compression or a disc that is truly damaged beyond natural repair, we may discuss surgical options. Minimally Invasive Spine Surgery: We use tiny incisions and advanced cameras to fix the problem with minimal disruption to your body. Disc Replacement: A modern way to maintain your neck\u2019s flexibility while removing the source of the pain. The recovery from these procedures is much faster than it used to be, and I will be with you every step of the way, from the first &#8220;hello&#8221; in the recovery room to your final check-up. Don&#8217;t choose your doctor randomly!Browse my personal website now and see the shoulder treatment conditions I offer professionally, as well as what previous clients have to say about them. Living in Dubai: Prevention and Lifestyle Tips We are lucky to live in such a dynamic city, but it comes with its own stresses. Here is how you can protect your neck and shoulders: The Eye-Level Rule: Keep your computer and phone at eye level. If you&#8217;re looking down, you&#8217;re putting 20-30 extra pounds of pressure on your neck! Stay Hydrated: Our discs<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":9965,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"elementor_theme","categories":[12],"tags":[90,92,89,91],"class_list":["post-10465","blogs","type-blogs","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-shoulder","tag-cervical-spine-health","tag-minimally-invasive-surgery","tag-neck-and-shoulder-doctor","tag-pinched-nerve"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/usamasaleh.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/blogs\/10465","targetHints":{"all